# =============================================================================
# Raw entry arguments — the list holds the arguments, not the program name
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `incipit argumenta <name>` without `@ cli` binds the raw argument list
#   • the list holds the arguments the program was given; the program name is
#     never an element, on every target
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • reading `args[0]` as the program name — it is the first argument
#
# See also: argumenta, incipit, cli
# =============================================================================

# EXPECTED stdout: see argumenta-raw-la.expected (run with arguments `a b`)

incipit argumenta args {
    nota args
}
